Give both models exactly the same SGG background, the same design problem, and the same instructions. Then compare their answers on architectural understanding, identifying problems, practical solutions, and whether they respect existing design decisions.
And there's one enormous fairness issue: Luma has accumulated a great deal of SGG history through our work together. A fresh Gemini session won't automatically have that. So we should give both contestants the same project brief, rather than compare Luma's memory against Gemini's ignorance.
